NAME
       sh - the PureC command shell

SYNOPSIS
       sh [-c COMMAND] [SCRIPT [ARG]...]

DESCRIPTION
       A POSIX style shell: pipes, redirections (> >> < 2>&1), variables,
       quoting, here documents, if/while/for/case, functions, command
       substitution $(...) and arithmetic $((...)). The interactive shell has a
       line editor with history and completion.

OPTIONS
       -c COMMAND
           run COMMAND and exit

LINE EDITING
       Left/Right, Home/End, Ctrl+A/E    move the cursor
       Up/Down                           browse history (saved in ~/.sh_history)
       Tab                               complete commands and paths
       Ctrl+U / Ctrl+K / Ctrl+W          delete to start / to end / previous word
       Ctrl+L                            clear the screen
       Ctrl+C                            cancel the line, or interrupt the running program
       Ctrl+D                            exit on an empty line

BUILT-IN COMMANDS
       cd pwd echo printf test [ export readonly unset set shift read eval exec exit return break continue
       trap umask type command kill wait source . true false : history

PROMPT
       PS1 understands \u user, \h host, \w directory, \W its last part, \$ (# for root),
       \e escape, \n newline and \[ \] around invisible sequences.

EXAMPLES
       sh -c "ls | wc -l"
       sh build.sh

SEE ALSO
       help(1), env(1), terminal(1)
